### BuildTrack — task API, and the RBAC proof
#
# PLAN.md §7 item 4: "RBAC enforced server-side, demonstrably — include a .http
# request showing a 403. Many candidates only hide buttons in the UI."
#
# The 403 blocks below are the point of this file. Every one of them is a
# request the UI would never send, because the button is hidden — and every one
# is refused by the API anyway.
#
# Run top to bottom: the @token variables are captured from the login calls.
# Seeded password for every demo account is `password123` (see prisma/seed.js).

@base = http://localhost:8000/api/v1

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Logins — one per role
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@buildtrack.com", "password": "password123" }

###
@admin = {{loginAdmin.response.body.token}}

# @name loginPm
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "pm@buildtrack.com", "password": "password123" }

###
@pm = {{loginPm.response.body.token}}

# @name loginStaff
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "engineer@buildtrack.com", "password": "password123" }

###
@staff = {{loginStaff.response.body.token}}

# @name loginClient
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "client@siamproperty.co.th", "password": "password123" }

###
@client = {{loginClient.response.body.token}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Reads — scoped by project membership
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### ADMIN sees every task
GET {{base}}/tasks?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### STAFF sees only tasks on projects they are staffed to (16 of 24 in the seed)
GET {{base}}/tasks?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}

### CLIENT sees only tasks on projects owned by their company
GET {{base}}/tasks?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{client}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Filters
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Top-level tasks only. `null` is a real filter and is NOT the same as
### omitting the param — the string "null" is converted to a SQL NULL.
GET {{base}}/tasks?parentTaskId=null&limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### The sub-tasks of one parent
GET {{base}}/tasks?parentTaskId=76
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Everything waiting to be checked — the PM's review queue
GET {{base}}/tasks?status=REVIEW
Authorization: Bearer {{pm}}

### My work, most urgent first
GET {{base}}/tasks?assignedToId=36&sort=-priority
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}

### Overdue and unfinished
GET {{base}}/tasks?dueBefore=2026-08-22&status=IN_PROGRESS
Authorization: Bearer {{pm}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 403 — the whole point of this file
###
### Set @ownTask to a task assigned to engineer@buildtrack.com, and
### @otherTask to one on the same project assigned to somebody else.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@ownTask = 96
@otherTask = 86
@foreignTask = 94

### 403 — STAFF cannot create tasks (requireRole)
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "projectId": 25, "name": "should never exist" }

### 403 — STAFF cannot delete tasks (requireRole)
DELETE {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}

### 200 — STAFF CAN move their own task along
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "IN_PROGRESS" }

### 403 — but NOT to APPROVED. Signing off your own work is exactly what the
### REVIEW state exists to prevent. This is a per-TRANSITION rule, so no
### role middleware can express it — see canTransitionStatus.
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "APPROVED" }

### 403 — and not on a task belonging to a colleague, even on their own project
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{otherTask}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "IN_PROGRESS" }

### 403 — same rule for progress
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{otherTask}}/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "progressPercent": 90 }

### 403 — a task on a project this user is not staffed to is invisible AND
### unreachable, not merely absent from the list
GET {{base}}/tasks/{{foreignTask}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staff}}

### 200 — a CLIENT's single permitted write in the entire application:
### approving finished work on their own project (WORKFLOWS.md U-3.9)
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{client}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "APPROVED" }

### 403 — and nothing else. A CLIENT cannot push work backwards,
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{client}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "IN_PROGRESS" }

### 403 — cannot report progress,
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{client}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "progressPercent": 100 }

### 403 — and cannot create work.
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{client}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "projectId": 25, "name": "nope" }


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 400 — validation
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 400 — progress is 0-100. The only numeric field a STAFF user can write,
### so its bounds are the whole guard.
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "progressPercent": 101 }

### 400 — you cannot assign work to someone who is not on the project team.
### Task visibility runs through membership, so this would create a task its
### own assignee could not see.
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assignedToId": 999999 }

### 400 — a task cannot be its own parent
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parentTaskId": {{ownTask}} }

### 400 — nor nest under a parent in a different project
PATCH {{base}}/tasks/{{ownTask}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parentTaskId": 76 }


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Write path — create a WBS, then tear it down
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# @name createParent
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{pm}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": 25,
  "name": "งานติดตั้งระบบไฟฟ้า",
  "description": "เดินสายไฟและติดตั้งตู้ควบคุมทั้งอาคาร",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "startDate": "2026-09-01",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-15"
}

###
@parentId = {{createParent.response.body.task.id}}

### Sub-task under it
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{pm}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": 25,
  "parentTaskId": {{parentId}},
  "name": "เดินท่อร้อยสาย",
  "priority": "MEDIUM"
}

### Deleting the parent cascades to its sub-tasks — parentTaskId is
### onDelete: Cascade in schema.prisma. The confirm dialog says so.
DELETE {{base}}/tasks/{{parentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{pm}}
